[lease] card | # Contributor host-only calibration; this is not the maintainer drive's reference band.
[lease] card | # Eight blocking workers can hide up to eight serial request latencies [derived ceiling,
[lease] card | # assuming equal requests and no bandwidth cap]. Shared bandwidth, CPU work and joining
[lease] card | # can leave the ratio near or below one. No inference speed is predicted by this card.
[lease] card | kind: calibration
[lease] card | question: how does this contributor's SSD read expert batches as blocking read workers increase?
[lease] card | term: probe_nvread k8 directN median GB/s at threads 8 divided by threads 1, same seed per round,
[lease] card |   alongside all cache/direct1/directN k1,k2,k4,k8 and contiguous range reference rows
[lease] card | unit: ratio
[lease] card | predict: 1.0..8.0
[lease] card | reason: collect a drive-specific worker-count curve and request-size reference for the paged verify IO term
[lease] card | condition: existing lease-hold runner with a contributor lock directory; no GPU timed or opened;
[lease] card |   existing probe_nvread mincore cold/full checks and aligned O_DIRECT reads; three rounds with rotated
[lease] card |   worker order and the same draws within each round; drive counters, pressure and foreign-process IO
[lease] card |   recorded around each child; neither drive/controller caches nor other services are reset;
[lease] card |   a read-byte reconciliation outside five percent marks the run contaminated, retaining its output
[lease] card | decide-in: carry the drive-specific curve into the paged IO discussion, separately from native inference
[lease] card | decide-below: examine worker overhead and recorded contention before proposing deeper IO queues
[lease] card | decide-above: audit byte accounting, warm-drive effects and the instrument before using the ratio
[lease] card: ok kind=calibration (no ruler: not an ab card)
